     I assume that slash'em is like nethack in this regard:
there is no template options file for the unix (including linux)
port.  You have to create that file from scratch.  The name you
found in the manual is undoubtedly accurate; the location would
be your home directory.  So you should create ~/.slashemrc with
a text editor and put whatever option settings in that.



